        "titles": [
          "Comparison of the Uniper Planning Case and the Net Zero Emissions (NZE)/"
        ],
        "subtitles": [
          "1.5-°C-Scenario"
        ],
        "paragraph": "Using the assumptions of the \"1.5°C\" scenario to model the implications for the European power and the global gas sector, Uniper could assess how its individual business lines would be affected in this scenario. The quantitative scenario analysis focused on Uniper's future operational segments:\n- Green Generation\n- Green Generation\n- Flexible Generation\n- **Greener Commodities**\nThe time horizon for the resilience test extends to 2040, differentiating the short to medium term as the period from 2023 until 2030, and long-term as the period between 2030 and 2040. The resilience test has been structured along the following four dimensions:\n- The general compatibility of the respective business lines with the \"1.5°C\" scenario.\n- The general compatibility of the respective business lines with the \"1.5°C\" scenario.\n- The general alignment potential of the respective business lines under the EU Taxonomy Regulation (Annex A, Climate-risk assessment for DNSH) currently and in the short-to-medium term, and potentially remaining ESG risks to which the respective business line would be exposed.\n- The financial impact on key earnings streams under the \"1.5°C\" scenario (quantitative assessment and semi-quantitative assessment).\n- The key climate-related transitional risks and opportunities as identified in the aforementioned expert workshops.",
        "classification": "EU Taxonomy",
        "report_name": "UNIPER_SE_NA_O.N.pdf"
      },
