        "subtitles": [
          "Minimum safeguards (MS)"
        ],
        "paragraph": "In its FAQ of June 2023, the European Commission for the first time specified concrete requirements for compliance with the minimum safeguards, which are laid down in Article 18 of Regulation (EU) 2020/852. In addition to the previously required compliance with the OECD Guidelines for Multinational Enterprises, the United Nations Guiding Principles on Business and Human Rights including the ILO Fundamental Principles and Rights at Work and the International Charter of Human Rights, a connection to the DNSH principle was established in accordance with the Sustainable Finance Disclosure Regulation (SFDR). In this context, the topics of human rights (including labour and consumer rights), anti-bribery and anti-corruption, taxation and fair competition were addressed. On the topic of human rights, IMMOFINANZ Group adheres to the six-step due diligence process to prevent significant harm according to the guidelines within the OECD Guidelines.",
