        "paragraph": "The proportion of Taxonomy-eligible capital expenditure (CapEx) is determined by dividing the Taxonomy-eligible capital expenditure by total additions to intangible and tangible assets. For further details, see note 10, table \"Intangible\" assets\" and note 11, table \"Property, plant and equipment (incl. right-of-use assets)\", lines \"Additions\".\nLikewise, to determine the proportion of Taxonomy-eligible operating expenditure (OpEx), the Taxonomy-eligible operating expenditure is divided by the Group's total operating expenditure. For further details, see note 6, table \"Composition of other operating expenses\".\nFor financial year 2023 we have not identified any Taxonomy-eligible capital or operating expenditure within the scope of application of the delegated acts.\nFor financial year 2023 we have not identified any economic activities at Deutsche Börse Group involving energy production from nuclear energy and fossil gas.",
