          "Operating expenditure"
        ],
        "subtitles": [],
        "paragraph": "Operating expenditure as defined by EU taxonomy take into account non-capitalizable expenses for research and development, renovation measures, shortterm lease, maintenance and other direct expenditure relating to the day-to-day servicing of assets of property, plant and equipment to ensure that the taxonomy-eligible or taxonomy-aligned assets are ready for operation. Operating expenditure cannot be reconciled directly to the presentation in the consolidated statement of income.\nOperating expenditure already identified as part of \"Revenues\" and attributable to taxonomyaligned economic activities was allocated as follows. Operating expenditure that could not be clearly allocated to a taxonomy-eligible or taxonomy-aligned business area were taken into account using an allocation key. The allocation key is based on the share of taxonomyaligned revenue per production site and is applied to the operating expenditure of the respective production site in the next step. This key was used to distribute 100% of the operating expenditure. No other significant operating expenditure from other activities was identified.\nY – yes, Taxonomy-eligible and Taxonomy-aligned activity with the relevant environmental objetive; N – no, Taxonomiy-eligible but not Taxonomy-aligned activity with the relevant environmental objetive;<br>N/EL – not eligible,",
