        "page_number": 176,
        "table_caption": "Turnover 2023",
        "paragraph": "The total reported turnover for 2023 amounted to EUR 626.7 million, of which EUR 603.5 million, representing 96.3% of the total, was classified as Taxonomy-eligible, and EUR 23.2 million, or 3.7%, as Taxonomy-non-eligible. Within the Taxonomy-eligible activities, there were no environmentally sustainable activities classified as Taxonomy-aligned (A.1), accounting for EUR 0 (0% of total turnover), with no proportion attributable to enabling or transitional activities, and maintaining 0% alignment for both 2023 and 2022. Conversely, Taxonomy-eligible activities not yet environmentally sustainable (A.2), representing EUR 603.5 million or 96.3% of total turnover, primarily consisted of 'Data-based solutions to reduce greenhouse gas emissions' (CCM 8.2). For this activity, the substantial contribution criterion for Climate Change Mitigation was assessed as 'N' (No), while for Climate Change Adaptation, Water, Circular Economy, Pollution, and Biodiversity, it was classified as 'N/EL' (Not Eligible). Consequently, as the substantial contribution criteria were not met, no further examination of the Do No Significant Harm (DNSH) criteria (across Climate Change Mitigation, Climate Change Adaptation, Water, Circular Economy, Pollution, Biodiversity) nor of the minimum safeguards was carried out for this activity. This category also showed 0% alignment for both 2023 and 2022 and was not classified as an enabling or transitional activity.",
        "classification": "EU taxonomy",
