        "table_caption": "OpEx (Operating Expenditure)",
        "paragraph": "For the fiscal year 2023/24, Zumtobel Group's total Operating Expenditure (OpEx) was TEUR 29,079. Of this, TEUR 28,924 (99% of total OpEx) was classified as Taxonomy-eligible, while TEUR 155 (1%) was Taxonomy-non-eligible. Within the Taxonomy-eligible OpEx, TEUR 4,963 (17% of total OpEx) was Taxonomy-aligned, and TEUR 23,961 (82% of total OpEx) was Taxonomy-eligible but not aligned.\n\nFor Taxonomy-aligned activities (A.1), 'Manufacture of energy efficiency equipment for buildings' (CCM-3.5) accounted for TEUR 4,957 (17% of total OpEx). This activity substantially contributes to Climate Change Mitigation ('Y') and is 'N/EL' for Climate Change Adaptation, Water, Pollution, Circular Economy, and Biodiversity. All six DNSH criteria were met ('Y'), and Minimum Safeguards were fulfilled ('Y'), classifying it as an 'Enabling' activity. 'Installation, maintenance and repair of charging stations for electric vehicles in buildings' (CCM-7.4) involved TEUR 6 (0% of total OpEx), substantially contributing to Climate Change Mitigation ('Y') and 'N/EL' for others. All DNSH criteria and Minimum Safeguards were met, classifying it as an 'Enabling' activity. The total Taxonomy-aligned OpEx (A.1) of TEUR 4,963 (17% of total OpEx) showed a 17% substantial contribution to Climate Change Mitigation and 0% for other objectives, consistently meeting all DNSH criteria and Minimum Safeguards. All of this, TEUR 4,963 (17% of total OpEx), was enabling, with 100% attributed to Climate Change Mitigation, and 0 TEUR (0% of total OpEx) was transitional, despite a 34% figure shown for Climate Change Mitigation within this category.\n\nFor Taxonomy-eligible but not environmentally sustainable activities (A.2), 'Manufacture of energy efficiency equipment for buildings' (CCM-3.5) involved TEUR 22,528 (77% of total OpEx), classified as 'EL' for Climate Change Mitigation and 'N/EL' for others. 'Installation, maintenance and repair of energy efficiency equipment' (CCM-7.3) accounted for TEUR 178 (1% of total OpEx), 'EL' for Climate Change Mitigation and 'N/EL' for others. 'Installation, maintenance and repair of instruments and devices for measuring, regulation and controlling energy performance of buildings' (CCM-7.5) was TEUR 1,255 (4% of total OpEx), 'EL' for Climate Change Mitigation and 'N/EL' for others. All these A.2 activities consistently met all DNSH criteria ('Y') and Minimum Safeguards ('Y'). The aggregated Taxonomy-eligible but not aligned OpEx (A.2) of TEUR 23,961 (82% of total OpEx) showed an 82% eligibility for Climate Change Mitigation and 0% for other objectives, consistently meeting all DNSH criteria and Minimum Safeguards.\n\nOverall, the total Taxonomy-eligible OpEx (A.1 + A.2) amounted to TEUR 28,924 (99% of total OpEx), demonstrating a 99% eligibility for Climate Change Mitigation and 0% for other objectives, with all DNSH criteria and Minimum Safeguards consistently met. According to the aggregated 2022/23 data for the DNSH section, the proportion of Taxonomy-aligned OpEx (A.1) was 9%, and the proportion of Taxonomy-eligible (A.1+A.2) was 63%.",
