        "paragraph": "This table details TAKKT's Capital Expenditure (CapEx) for the 2023 fiscal year, totaling 30,681 TEUR. All of this amount (100%) was identified as taxonomy-relevant. From the taxonomy-relevant CapEx, 17,807 TEUR (58%) was classified as taxonomy-eligible, while 12,874 TEUR (42%) was not taxonomy-eligible. Consistent with the company's reporting, no CapEx was deemed environmentally sustainable (taxonomy-aligned) for either 2023 or 2022, reflected by 0% for the 'Taxonomy-aligned proportion of CapEx' for both years. For the taxonomy-aligned activities, specifically 'Electricity generation using solar photovoltaic technology' (4.1), 'Transport by motorbikes, passenger cars and light commercial vehicles' (6.5), 'Installation, maintenance and repair of energy efficiency equipment' (7.3), 'Installation, maintenance and repair of charging stations for electric vehicles in buildings (and parking spaces attached to buildings)' (7.4), 'Acquisition and ownership of buildings' (7.7), and 'Data processing, hosting and related activities' (8.1), all substantial contribution criteria (Climate change mitigation, Climate change adaptation, Sustainable use and protection of water and marine resources, Circular economy, Pollution prevention and control, Protection and restoration of biodiversity and ecosystems) showed a 0% contribution. Furthermore, all these activities received a 'No' (N) designation across all 'Do Not Significantly Harm' (DNSH) criteria (Climate change mitigation, Climate change adaptation, Water & marine resources, Circular economy, Pollution, Biodiversity & ecosystems, Minimum safeguards). The taxonomy-eligible but not environmentally sustainable CapEx (17,807 TEUR, 58%) was allocated to: 'Acquisition and ownership of buildings' (14,191 TEUR, 46.3%), 'Transport by motorbikes, passenger cars and light commercial vehicles' (1,845 TEUR, 6.0%), 'Electricity generation using solar photovoltaic technology' (1,409 TEUR, 4.6%), 'Data processing, hosting and related activities' (152 TEUR, 0.5%), 'Installation, maintenance and repair of energy efficiency equipment' (124 TEUR, 0.4%), and 'Installation, maintenance and repair of charging stations for electric vehicles in buildings (and parking spaces attached to buildings)' (86 TEUR, 0.3%). No activities were classified as 'enabling' or 'transitional' in this reporting segment.",
