        "paragraph": "Wienerberger comprehensively addresses the 'Do No Significant Harm' (DNSH) criteria for the EU Taxonomy's environmental objectives. For climate change adaptation, climate risk analyses, based on RCP 4.5 and RCP 8.5 scenarios, are conducted at all production sites, leading to site-specific adaptation solutions. Regarding sustainable use of water and marine resources, taxonomy-eligible sites assess production impact and implement water management plans in line with local regulations. In terms of circular economy, the company analyzes activities for reuse of secondary raw materials, durability, recyclability, waste management, and substances of concern and their traceability, ensuring no significant harm; notably, ceramic building materials, made from natural clay sediments, contribute to this objective. Pollution prevention and control are managed through regular reporting and external monitoring of manufacturing processes' environmental impact. Lastly, for the protection and restoration of biodiversity, production sites analyze their immediate environmental impact, developing biodiversity action plans where necessary to ensure protection.",
