        ],
        "paragraph": "Upgrading employees' skills is an important factor in the company's success. With this in mind, the motto for 2023 was #freenetlernt and the development of employees' learning hours was included as a corporate goal in the variable remuneration of the Executive Board and employees. As a result, formal learning hours per employee increased by over 30% to an average of 12.9 hours in 2023 (previous year: 9.8 hours) [GRI 404-1]. The target of a minimum learning time of eleven hours was thus clearly exceeded. This target is to be maintained in the future - regardless of its relevance to remuneration.",
