      "question": "Why are fixed interest financial instruments more vulnerable to market rate changes than floating rate instruments, and how does AGRANA address this vulnerability to align with ESG risk management practices?",
      "answer": "Fixed interest financial instruments are more vulnerable to market rate changes because their interest rates remain constant, making their value susceptible to fluctuations in market rates, unlike floating rate instruments that adjust frequently.",
