          "**NMP-free removers**"
        ],
        "paragraph": "The production process for semiconductor devices requires numerous cleaning steps to remove the photoresists used to pattern the circuit design. These cleaning methods require complex solvent chemistries that selectively remove these photoresists without damaging the sensitive electronic components.\nIn many cases, however, the most effective solvents also pose significant environmental hazards. For example, NMP, a mainstream solvent common in wafer cleaning, is highly toxic and classified as an SVHC (Substance of Very High Concern) under the European Union's REACH regulation. In response, we have continued expanding our portfolio of formulated cleaners and have committed to not using NMP in new product development.",
        "classification": "ESG",
        "report_name": "Merck_KGaA.pdf"
      },
