        ],
        "paragraph": "As part of the budget process and strategic sparring, 93% of INDUS Holding AG's portfolio companies formulated emissions reduction goals up to the target year 2026 (SS01-ET). The portfolio companies that were added in the 2022 financial year have since set emissions reduction targets, and only a few portfolio companies felt unable to formulate well-founded reduction plans due to uncertain framework conditions. Seven projects were supported by the sustainability development bank in 2023, which is one more than in the previous year. This involved EUR 1.1 million in funding being approved for the portfolio companies, with an underlying investment volume of EUR 2.7 million. This corresponds to an average funding rate of 41%.\n\\* To clarify the starting point and the target progress regarding the greenhouse gas reduction target (PEO1-GHG), the gross emission intensity for the 2018 base year is stated (before taking account of emission offsetting). The other information on emissions intensity in the PE01-GHG KPI refers to net emissions intensity. All other information on greenhouse gas emissions in the table refers to gross emissions.",
